/* Revision 06: local, stateful design previews of the revised requirements.
 * Knowledge: entries -> managed documents -> passages/index history/share/move.
 * Settings: add-ons, trust, paths, containers, RAG and updates. Help is local.
 * External effects and inference are simulated; imported bytes stay in IndexedDB.
 */
const vdSettingsTopics=[['General','General & repository paths','project'],['Safety','Access & safety','review'],['Containers','Containers','layers'],['Knowledge','Documents & retrieval','book'],['Addons','Add-ons','layers'],['Updates','App updates','history']];
wbSettingsTopics.unshift(vdSettingsTopics[0]);wbSettingsTopics.splice(4,0,vdSettingsTopics[1]);wbSettingsTopics.push(...vdSettingsTopics.slice(2));
const vdHelpGuides={
 chat:['Workspace coordinator','Start here to ask about any project, feature, issue, pull request or agent. The workspace coordinator inspects current records and links its answers to the work.','Choose a session from the right sidebar or start a new conversation. Every input supports file selection, drop and paste, plus a model selector. The router pins the resolved model for the session.','Use a work link to inspect an assignment, its coordinator, transcripts and artifacts. Redirect active work at the next safe step; user directions and configured permissions remain authoritative.'],
 overview:['Projects & repositories','A project can contain multiple repositories. Features may coordinate changes across those repositories, while standalone issues live directly in the project.','The project queue ranks features and standalone issues together. Keep working is off by default; when enabled it claims one eligible item at a time and creates a fresh coordinator session for each item. No eligible work stops the mode until manually restarted.','Project defaults can override repository locations and container preferences. Archiving with active agents requires confirmation and then stops all project work immediately. Restoring a project leaves its work and schedules stopped.'],
 feature:['Planning & autonomous work','A feature owns a plan, planning cards, coordinator, sessions, worktrees and delivery history. Refine the plan at any time. The approved plan stays active while a revision awaits approval; approval replaces it and rejection leaves it unchanged.','An incomplete plan needs approval before implementation. After approval the coordinator may adapt delegation and task grouping within that scope, filling useful parallel work up to the per-feature cap (default 10). Issues have their own independent cap; there is no global agent-count cap.','Tasks integrate through PRs to a feature branch. All final repository PRs must pass checks and reviews before any are merged; merge in dependency order. Complete the feature after all final PRs are verified merged. Releases and deployments remain separate.'],
 knowledge:['Knowledge & managed documents','Knowledge, lessons and memory form one tagged collection. General lessons can be shared; project knowledge and conventions remain project-scoped.','Documents supports Markdown, plain text, PDF and Word. An import keeps a managed project artifact, independent of the original file. Index removal preserves that artifact. Share explicitly or move the same document to another project.','Extract existing text first. Scanned pages use the configured routed vision fallback, enabled by default. Embedding and vision inference both use the router. Partial extraction, errors and stale indexes remain visible. Search results retain source and page or heading locators.'],
 plugins:['Creating a harness package','Language packs and harness extensions are managed executables. Installing a compatible prebuilt package does not rebuild DevWorks or require a Rust compiler. Building a Rust package locally requires its development toolchain.','Declare version, compatibility, dependencies and contributions. Extensions may contribute tools, commands, workflows, verification gates, events, context, roles, skills, native host-rendered panels and router adapters. Protocol and SDK details are still to be designed.','Agent-authored packages and updates require approval tied to the reviewed version before activation. Retain the previous version for rollback; approved changes adopt at a safe boundary. All brokered actions use shared permissions and the router. Executable separation alone is not an OS sandbox.'],
 testing:['Architecture & testing','Clean, purposeful boundaries and shared application operations serve both UI and agents. Document responsibilities, contracts, invariants and difficult interactions alongside the code.','Unit tests and integration tests use deterministic provider substitutes and must NOT execute real inference, including tiny or synthetic models. Exercise important behavior, concurrency, failure, cancellation and recovery without a numerical coverage target.','Real-inference end-to-end tests will be set up later as a distinct suite. Maintain editable structural and workflow diagrams with the code, including detailed plugin lifecycle and failure paths. The diagrams in this UI study are conceptual navigation aids, not implemented contracts.'],
 recovery:['Pauses & recovery','Closing the main window pauses and persists work, then exits. After reopening, manually Continue selected features and issues. Sleep and wake while the app stays open continue active work automatically.','Enabled schedules reactivate; interrupted scheduled runs resume the same run automatically. Missed occurrences stay missed, and overlapping inference occurrences are skipped.','Before retrying a state-changing operation, reconcile whether it already happened. Unknown outcomes pause only affected work and dependents, with required input and a notification; unrelated work can continue.'],
 safety:['Access & tool safety','Choose tool availability and a trust profile in Settings. Full access never removes read-only reviewer rules, explicit approvals, destructive-operation guards or the prohibition on force-pushing main.','Guard destructive calls before dispatch to prevent accidental whole-drive or repository deletion. A blocked operation needs visible rationale and work attribution. Rules and OS enforcement still require architecture validation.','Managed executables run code. Brokered permission checks do not by themselves confine arbitrary native file or network access. Do not treat worktrees or the UI preview as a security sandbox.'],
 updates:['App updates','DevWorks checks SceneWorks/DevWorks GitHub Releases every hour while open and downloads available updates in the background. The installed version stays visible in the lower-left sidebar.','Installation and restart require explicit approval. A downloaded update never counts as approval. Preserve work and apply manual selective resume for features and issues after restart.','The app and installed add-ons bundle matching local Help. Search and read documentation offline without remote embedding or a hosted documentation service.']
};
